From 310b1bd37a97b58a8e081841c58cc638e60fb600 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:36:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/28] settings: load secrets from a root-provided env file,
 refuse insecure defaults

- SECRET_KEY and ZIP_PASSWORD are required. Startup fails with
  ImproperlyConfigured when either is missing, too short, or still set
  to the value published in upstream settings.py/docker-compose.yml.
- RDGEN_ENV_FILE (e.g. /etc/rdgen/rdgen.env, root:rdgen 0640) is parsed
  into a private dict, not os.environ, so its values do not appear in
  /proc/<pid>/environ. Real environment variables still take precedence.
- ALLOWED_HOSTS and CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS come from the environment. The
  ALLOWED_HOSTS default is localhost instead of '*'.
- Data (SQLite DB, builds) lives under RDGEN_DATA_DIR, outside the
  root-owned code tree.
- Upload limits: DATA_UPLOAD_MAX_MEMORY_SIZE is 8 MiB instead of
  unlimited.
- Optional sub-path mount via RDGEN_URL_PREFIX (FORCE_SCRIPT_NAME). The
  session and CSRF cookies get their own names and path so they cannot
  collide with a console served from the same host.
- RDGEN_GITHUB_API is configurable (https only; plain http is allowed for
  localhost stubs in tests).
- Security headers: X-Frame-Options DENY, same-origin referrer policy.
  Logging goes to stderr.

GENURL/PROTOCOL/SH_SECRET stay as inert placeholders until the pull-model
commits remove their last users.

